{"id": "EUVD-2026-76367", "enisaUuid": "61b6406e-dea5-3716-934d-89907f6ab1b7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: supply: max17040: synchronize work cancellation on suspend\n\nmax17040_work() requeues itself after every poll. cancel_delayed_work()\nonly cancels a pending instance and does not wait for a callback that is\nalready running.\n\nIf system suspend races with the polling callback, the callback can\ncontinue accessing the fuel gauge and requeue itself after the suspend\ncallback returns.\n\nUse cancel_delayed_work_sync() to ensure polling is quiesced before\nsuspend completes.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:47:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bd453e328a0325f838c3bf64d4609c6c1866ed7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a9ec6707b545b2a0b35942c8b68d975cb901f77", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc946222e4b5bdb4e92bc3a5a5e8fc4ddac34ec0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23783db5642a714f0547c5b5b0c9cdbb1be7b084", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a863417fb9a1034ab1cfe4fa0de46ce1f95f3ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aad7247bd35ad44af90a5e8974cdff614235b497", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36e6ce0f402f965328b27fd31ac793110e8a0c39", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86a3a8a926aa5969c329d1df2d3259f189961bbc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5fpq-2c4w-2f7x", "CVE-2026-89461"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03ecad96-2fc6-3311-83ba-549d606871d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "05705983-39b0-35e0-993a-a661424205c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2185c115-3e9a-3d8d-929d-90946f27cebe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c6f4a42de60b981dd210de01cd3e575835e3158e <23783db5642a714f0547c5b5b0c9cdbb1be7b084"}, {"id": "366f35e7-0c7a-3b